  "schema_version": 1,
  "jsp": "JSP-000588",
  "erdos": 720,
  "title": "How fast do the two-color size Ramsey numbers of prescribed paths and cycles grow?",
  "scope": "For two-color size Ramsey numbers defined by the least edge count of actual finite hosts, paths of n edges and cycles of n edges have eventual O(n) upper bounds. Therefore the proposed path/n divergence is false, and both path/n^2 and cycle/n^2 tend to 0. All sufficiently large n, including both cycle parities, are covered.",
  "attribution": "Existing plby/lean-proofs source. Primary header credits Jozsef Beck for the informal result and Codex / GPT-5.6 Sol for formalization (original accents preserved in copied source). All 23 sources and their notices are preserved byte-for-byte. No uploader-as-original-author, priority, recipient or new-proof claim.",
